@@ -68,0 +69,33 @@ The CPU regression suite runs in the ordinary `npm test` CI gate. Its response e
+## Organization directory (`/organization/`)
+
+The site serves a vendored, hash-pinned copy of the reviewed `Pick-Your-AI/.github` organization bundle
+(`public/organization/`, pinned in `contracts/organization/PIN.json`; contract in
+[docs/ORGANIZATION_DIRECTORY.md](../ORGANIZATION_DIRECTORY.md)). It deploys like any other change: the bundle is part of
+`site-dist`, and a changed bundle is a new website commit.
+
+- `.htaccess` serves `.mmd` as `text/plain` and relaxes only `style-src` (to `'self' 'unsafe-inline'`) under
+  `/organization/`. The canonical page embeds one `<style>` block and its SVG exports carry inline styles.
+  `script-src` stays `'self'`; the rest of the site keeps `style-src 'self'`. Drop the exception when the generator
+  ships an external stylesheet.
+- `verify-live.sh` section 7 reads the pin of the release being verified. If a bundle is admitted it checks that the
+  actual `GET /organization/` response is **byte-identical to the pinned `index.html`** (not just a marker), the
+  effective CSP of every enforced policy (`scripts/deploy/organization-live.mjs`: `script-src` exactly `'self'`,
+  `script-src-elem`/`-attr` not widened, only `style-src` relaxed), the `/organization` redirect, and every file's
+  HTTP 200, MIME type and SHA-256 against the pin. If none is admitted it expects the pending SPA page and a real 404 for
+  `/organization/directory.js`. A rollback passes the target release's pin (`ORGANIZATION_PIN`); a target that predates
+  the integration has none and the section is skipped.
+- **Hosting gate.** The shared host currently injects its own monitoring (an inline script and an external script from
+  the host provider's CDN) into HTML responses. The CSP blocks their execution but cannot keep the bytes identical, so
+  the exact-bytes check on `/organization/` fails by design until the site is opted out of host-injected monitoring and
+  byte equality is verified. Do not weaken the check or strip injected content to pass a deployment. That is a hosting
+  account action for the owner; no one has authorized the website worker to take it.
+- Publication time is the time of the successful readback in the **Verify live site through Cloudflare** step. The
+  bundle's own observation time is older and says nothing about deployment.
+- Roll back a bad bundle like any release (`rollback_to=<sha>`), or revert the admitting PR.
+- `.github/workflows/organization-update-proposal.yml` is a prepared, **disabled** manual-dispatch route. It cannot
+  open a pull request until the owners settle a writer (the repository setting that lets Actions create pull
+  requests is off; a separate narrowly scoped identity is the alternative) and confirm the `contrib/…` branch name,
+  then set `ORGANIZATION_PROPOSAL_ENABLED`. Until then proposals come from an authorized human running the importer.
+- Run the helper's tests with `node --test scripts/deploy/organization-live.test.mjs` (add it to the CI test script
+  together with the pinned expectation in `live-admission.test.mjs`).
+
